3370: torus strata and Euler number \(8se\).
3371: 
3372: The quadratic deck is monomial on the central strata.
3373: Indeed on the source nodal identity torus it is
3374: \(Z\mapsto uZ^{-1}\), with a nonzero central unit
3375: \(u\).  It commutes with the scalar circle on the line,
3376: so in a line frame it sends \(V\mapsto f(Z)V\).
3377: The source, line and their linearization are algebraic,
3378: and this central torus map is regular and invertible.
3379: Thus \(f\) is a unit of \(\mathbb C[Z,Z^{-1}]\),
3380: so \(f(Z)=vZ^j\).  The induced maps on preserved
3381: boundary torus strata are the restrictions of this same
3382: integral monomial map.  Nonpreserved strata are permuted.
3383: An invariant refinement can be used for descent; every
3384: subdivision increases the number of maximal cones and
3385: does not lower the preceding root Euler count.
3386: 
3387: There is also an explicit invariant unimodular height-one
3388: choice, without a restriction to the rank-one generator
3389: marking.  Write the actual monomial deck on valuations as
3390: \(R(x,y)=(-x,y-jx)\), with \(j\in\mathbb Z\).
3391: It sends the source period \(h=(2s,\alpha)\) to
3392: \(-h\); comparison of the second coordinate gives
3393: \[
3394:                          j=\alpha/s.
3395: \]
3396: Thus the integrality of this shear follows from the
3397: actual deck morphism.  The whole-zero identity is now
3398: \(2\beta+cj=4e\).  For odd \(j\), the integral
3399: shear \(y'=y-(j-1)x/2\) gives
3400: \(R(x,y')=(-x,y'-x)\).  The positive unit-square
